.TH SDL_GetCameraFormat 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetCameraFormat \- Get the spec that a camera is using when generating images.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_camera.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_GetCameraFormat(SDL_Camera *camera, SDL_CameraSpec *spec);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Note that this might not be the native format of the hardware, as SDL might be converting to this format behind the scenes\[char46]
.PP
If the system is waiting for the user to approve access to the camera, as some platforms require, this will return false, but this isn\(aqt necessarily a fatal error; you should either wait for an
.BR SDL_EVENT_CAMERA_DEVICE_APPROVED
(or
.BR SDL_EVENT_CAMERA_DEVICE_DENIED )
event, or poll
.BR SDL_GetCameraPermissionState ()
occasionally until it returns non-zero\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I camera
opened camera device\[char46]
.TP
.I spec
the
.BR SDL_CameraSpec
to be initialized by this function\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_OpenCamera (3)
